What a “Pool”
A storage box that keeps already-created GameObjects so you can reuse them instead of creating new ones.
////////////////////////////
WHY pooling exists
Instantiate() is expensive.
If you use it many times per second → lag.
So instead of creating new objects every time, pooling does this:
  ----------------------------------->
Create object once → store it → reuse it → store again → reuse again

POOL BOX
┌────────────┐
│  Electron1 │  ← saved, deactivated
│  Electron2 │
│  Ring1     │
└────────────┘
Note:-
A pool reduces lag and reduces memory garbage creation by reusing objects instead of Instantiating/Destorying repeatedly.

What happens when we use pool.ContainsKey(key)?
-->
if (!pool.ContainsKey(key))
{
    pool[key] = new Queue<GameObject>();
}
✔ Step 1 — What does ContainsKey mean?
ContainsKey(key) simply asks: "Does this Dictionary already have this key?"
It returns:
true → key exists
false → key does NOT exist
✔ Step 2 — What is Dequeue()?
 -->Dequeue() removes the front object from the queue and returns it
 Step 3 — What is Enqueue()?
 Enqueue() adds an object to the back of the queue.
 Take → Use → Return → Take → Use → Return

 Why we use key as string :-
Because -> ⭐ Summary (simple)

We use string as the key because:
It is readable
It matches prefab names
It avoids confusion
It is easy to maintain
It supports unlimited pool categories

Q.1-> Why use ONE ObjectPooler for bullets/enemies/smoke
Core answer (one sentence):
One central ObjectPooler gives a single place to create, reuse, and manage pooled objects so your game uses less memory, has fewer bugs, and is easier to control and tune.
Note:-
We use a single ObjectPooler because it gives one central place to create, reuse, and manage all pooled objects for bullets, enemies, and effects


// pooling Concept 
using System.Collections.Generic;
using UnityEngine;

public class Objectpooler : MonoBehaviour 
{
	private readonly Dictionary<string , Queue<GameObject>> pool = new Dictionary<string , Queue<GameObject>();
	
	public void Createpool(String key , GameObject prefabs , int initalSize)
	{
		if(string.IsNullOrEmpty(key) || prefabs == null || initalSize < 0) return ;
		if(pool.ContainsKey(key)) return ;
		
		//creating a Queue for Object storage 
		var q = new Queue<GameObject>();
		for(int i = 0 ; i < initalSize ; i++)
		{
			GameObject go = instantiate(prefabs);
			go.name  = $"{key}_pooled{i}";
			go.setActive(false);
			q.Enque(go);
		}
		
		pool[key] = q ;
	}
	
	
	public GameObject SpawanFromPool(string key , vector3 postion Quaterian rotation )
	{
		if(!pool.ContainsKey(key))
		{
			Debug.log(" The pooled is nit found");
			return null;
		}
		Queue<GameObject> q = pool[key] ;
		GameObject obj ;
		if(q.count == 0 )
		{
			obj = new GameObject($"{key}_pooled")
		}
		else{
			obj =  q.Dequeue();
		}
		obj.setActive(true);
		obj.transform.postion = positin ;
		obj.rotation = rotation ;
		
		return obj ;
	}
	
	public void ReturnTopool(string key , GameObject obj)
	{
		if(string.IsNullOrEmpty(key) || obj == null ) return ;
		if(!pool.ContainsKey(key)
		{
			pool[key] = new Queue<GameObject>();
		}
		obj.setActive(false);
		pool[key].Enque(obj);
	}
	
	
}
